 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "3BEQVVI0CrgJ",
   "from": "Alison Rachel Marklein",
   "author": "1db25e6037654659",
   "date": "2014-12-22T15:58:53Z",
   "subject": "Accessing t-1 in ode model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hey everyone,<div><br><div>I am building a semi-discrete model and need to access time t-1 in my ode model. I have tried using a counter and an outside vector, but the variable at t-1 is always NA or 0. Has anyone else run into this problem, or been able to access previous values in a differential equation model? Thanks for the help!</div><div><br></div><div>Best, </div><div>Alison</div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "2_pT8GjjfSsJ",
   "from": "Noam Ross",
   "author": "8c8f0ca54c4a2459",
   "date": "2014-12-22T16:39:06Z",
   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: Accessing t-1 in ode model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);border:none;line-height:1.2;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Hi Rachel,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">If you are just looking to access the variable <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">t</code>, I’m not sure why you wouldn’t be able to access it in a normal <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">f(t, y, parms, ...)</code> derivative function.  However, the normal way to access lagged variables is to use the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">dede()</code> (delay differential equation) function.  See <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">?dede</code> for more details, but basically you access previous values with the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">lagvalue()</code> and <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">lagderiv()</code> calls, e.g., calling <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">lagvalue(t-1)</code> inside your derivative function returns a vector of state variables from <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">t-1</code>. Note you need to use some sort of <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">if</code> statement to deal with <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">t &lt; 0</code>.  There are good examples in the help file.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Noam</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGkgUmFjaGVsLDxicj48YnI+SWYgeW91IGFyZSBqdXN0IGxvb2tpbmcgdG8gYWNjZXNzIHRoZSB2\r\nYXJpYWJsZSBgdGAsIEknbSBub3Qgc3VyZSB3aHkgeW91IHdvdWxkbid0IGJlIGFibGUgdG8gYWNj\r\nZXNzIGl0IGluIGEgbm9ybWFsIGBmKHQsIHksIHBhcm1zLCAuLi4pYCBkZXJpdmF0aXZlIGZ1bmN0\r\naW9uLiDCoEhvd2V2ZXIsIHRoZSBub3JtYWwgd2F5IHRvIGFjY2VzcyBsYWdnZWQgdmFyaWFibGVz\r\nIGlzIHRvIHVzZSB0aGUgYGRlZGUoKWAgKGRlbGF5IGRpZmZlcmVudGlhbCBlcXVhdGlvbikgZnVu\r\nY3Rpb24uIMKgU2VlIGA/ZGVkZWAgZm9yIG1vcmUgZGV0YWlscywgYnV0IGJhc2ljYWxseSB5b3Ug\r\nYWNjZXNzIHByZXZpb3VzIHZhbHVlcyB3aXRoIHRoZSBgbGFndmFsdWUoKWAgYW5kIGBsYWdkZXJp\r\ndigpYCBjYWxscywgZS5nLiwgY2FsbGluZyBgbGFndmFsdWUodC0xKWAgaW5zaWR