     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon Dec 22 2014 at 7:58:54 AM Alison Rachel Marklein &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">alison....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hey everyone,<div><br><div>I am building a semi-discrete model and need to access time t-1 in my ode model. I have tried using a counter and an outside vector, but the variable at t-1 is always NA or 0. Has anyone else run into this problem, or been able to access previous values in a differential equation model? Thanks for the help!</div><div><br></div><div>Best, </div><div>Alison</div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
